# Naming

## Files

- Non-component modules: `kebab-case.ts` / `kebab-case.tsx` (e.g. `element-utils.ts`).
- React components: `PascalCase.tsx` (e.g. `LayerUI.tsx`).
- Tests next to source: `SameBaseName.test.tsx`.

## React

- Component functions: `PascalCase`.
- Props type for component `Foo`: `FooProps`.
- Hooks: `use` + camelCase description, e.g. `useCanvasPointer`.
- Prefer readable boolean props: `isOpen`, `hasSelection`, `shouldPersist`.

## TypeScript symbols

- Variables, functions, methods, properties: `camelCase`.
- Types, interfaces, enums: `PascalCase`.
- Generic type parameters: single uppercase or `TItem`-style when clarity helps (`T`, `K`, `TElement`).

## Module-level constants

- Tune numbers, flags, and shared literals often use `UPPER_SNAKE` in this codebase (e.g. `SCROLLBAR_WIDTH`).
- Structured or exported singleton-like objects may use `PascalCase` (e.g. font face lists). Match the surrounding package.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — file AppHelpers.tsx for a non-component module
// ✅ GOOD — app-helpers.ts

// ❌ BAD
const Default_color = "#000";

// ✅ GOOD
const defaultColor = "#000";

// ❌ BAD — boolean prop
<Foo open={true} />

// ✅ GOOD
<Foo isOpen={true} />
```

## How to verify

- `yarn test:typecheck` — catches many symbol and export issues.
- `yarn fix` — ESLint and formatting; rename drift often shows up in import paths or duplicate basenames.
- In review: match file basenames to role (kebab-case modules vs `PascalCase` components), `Foo` ↔ `FooProps`, and `use*` for hooks.
